  "body": "This PR integrates the `Document-Isolation-Policy` and `Document-Isolation-Policy-Report-Only` HTTP\nresponse headers (formerly incubated in https://wicg.github.io/document-isolation-policy/) into the\nHTML Standard, allowing individual documents to opt into cross-origin isolation without requiring\nCOOP and COEP across the entire browsing context group.\nCompanion Fetch PR: [whatwg/fetch PR](https://github.com/whatwg/fetch/pull/1981)\n### Summary of changes (organized into 4 commits)\n1. **Header, policy container, and inheritance:**\n   - Adds definitions for the various Document Isolation Policy struts and headers.\n   - Adds Document Isolation Policy to the PolicyContainer for inheritance management.\n   - Handles inheritance for workers (Dedicated Workers inherit DIP from their creator, all other workers ignore it).\n2. **Agent cluster cross-origin isolation keying:**\n   - Replaces the browsing context group's cross-origin isolation mode with an\n     agent cluster cross-origin isolation key.\n3. **Same-origin, cross-agent-cluster synchronous access checks:**\n   - Because Document Isolation Policy can place two same-origin Document inside the same\n     browsing context group into different agent clusters, updates synchronous access checks to also\n     require matching agents.\n4. **cross-origin isolated capability:**\n   - Exempts documents with an isolating Document Isolation Policy from requiring the\n     \"cross-origin-isolated\" permissions policy feature (so cross-origin widgets can isolate\n     themselves without embedder `allow=\"cross-origin-isolated\"`).\n\n### Checklist\n- [ ] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * Chromium (implemented)\n   * WebKit / Gecko: …\n- [ ] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/tree/master/html/document-isolation-policy (currently `.tentative`; follow-up WPT PR will remove `.tentative`)\n- [ ] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chromium: …\n   * Gecko: …\n   * WebKit: …\n   * Deno: N/A\n   * Node.js: N/A\n- [x] Corresponding [HTML AAM](https://w3c.github.io/html-aam/) & [ARIA in HTML](https://w3c.github.io/html-aria/) issues & PRs: N/A\n- [ ] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed: …\n- [x] The top of this comment includes a [clear commit message](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/COMMITTING.md) to use.\n- [ ] IANA registration request for `Document-Isolation-Policy` and `Document-Isolation-Policy-Report-Only`\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13326/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 25, 2026, 3:25 PM UTC (616e068)\">/acknowledgements.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13326/e8167f8...616e068/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 25, 2026, 3:25 PM UTC (616e068)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13326/browsers.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 25, 2026, 3:25 PM UTC (616e068)\">/browsers.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13326/e8167f8...616e068/browsers.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 25, 2026, 3:25 PM UTC (616e068)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13326/browsing-the-web.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 25, 2026, 3:25 PM UTC (616e068)\">/browsing-the-web.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13326/e8167f8...616e068/browsing-the-web.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 25, 2026, 3:25 PM UTC (616e068)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13326/document-lifecycle.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 25, 2026, 3:25 PM UTC (616e068)\">/document-lifecycle.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13326/e8167f8...616e068/document-lifecycle.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 25, 2026, 3:25 PM UTC (616e068)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13326/document-sequences.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 25, 2026, 3:25 PM UTC (616e068)\">/document-sequences.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13326/e8167f8...616e068/document-sequences.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 25, 2026, 3:25 PM UTC (616e068)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13326/index.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 25, 2026, 3:25 PM UTC (616e068)\">/index.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13326/e8167f8...616e068/index.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 25, 2026, 3:25 PM UTC (616e068)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13326/indices.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 25, 2026, 3:25 PM UTC (616e068)\">/indices.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13326/e8167f8...616e068/indices.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 25, 2026, 3:25 PM UTC (616e068)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13326/nav-history-apis.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 25, 2026, 3:25 PM UTC (616e068)\">/nav-history-apis.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13326/e8167f8...616e068/nav-history-apis.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 25, 2026, 3:25 PM UTC (616e068)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13326/semantics.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 25, 2026, 3:25 PM UTC (616e068)\">/semantics.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13326/e8167f8...616e068/semantics.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 25, 2026, 3:25 PM UTC (616e068)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13326/webappapis.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 25, 2026, 3:25 PM UTC (616e068)